// P03.26: long chains of selectors, calls, indexes, slices, type assertions,
// `*`, parentheses and mixes of them, in Go++ mode. The checker used to recurse once
// per link (a chain of about 600 selectors overflowed the stack of a
// sanitizer build); the links of a long chain are now evaluated in a loop
// (Checker::prepareChain), and the checking runs on a thread with a large
// stack (the nested calls `g(g(g(...)))` of the parser's deepest nesting have
// no chain to walk). Each form is generated by Inputs/gen-chain-stress.py at
// the depth the parser accepts (it stops at 1024 levels with E0031, see
// chain-bad.test). One function per form; chain-forms-go.long.test runs Go
// mode, chain-many.long.test 150 functions per form.
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-chains.py %gopp %t.d forms-gopp
